  "findings": [
    "Guard projects obtain NuGet auditing only from the root Directory.Build.props (P5 must carry an equal-or-stronger baseline, D14).",
    "Guard projects build only because docs/Directory.Packages.props disables central package management; any location outside docs/ inherits the root CPM and fails with NU1008.",
    "No global.json: the SDK floats (CI setup-dotnet 10.0.x; local 10.0.303).",
    "No NuGet.config: package sources come from user/machine configuration.",
    "No packages.lock.json and no locked restore; transitive dependencies are not pinned.",
    "Default bin/ and obj/ output inside docs/guards (ignored by Git, still written into the source tree).",
    "LayerGuard references ModelContextProtocol and Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting because the engine is also the legacy MCP server; this widens the trusted build dependency surface."
  ]
